Track 2: "Is the current thread taut?"
- Story & Context: Kora stands in the middle of the machinery room, clutching a spool of frayed copper wire while the lighthouse alarm pulses a warning cadence against the rhythm of her frantic heart. She confesses to the radio receiver that she has stopped the rotation of the beacon, hoping the darkness will force the ocean to speak its true name. "The bobbin screams for what we held."
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: A close-up of a woman's hands, frost-bitten and stained with machine grease, meticulously unraveling a glowing, energized bundle of golden wire against a backdrop of deep indigo darkness.

Track 3: The Mending of Svalbard
- Story & Context: Long after the station fell, sailors report that the ghosts of the lighthouse keepers walk the water during the equinox, carrying heavy nets woven from radio waves. They are said to be repairing the broken line of the horizon, singing the final movement of a song that never ends. "Woven breath anchors the tide."
